## Whole-Body Control (WBC)

### Task-Space Inverse Dynamics

**Objective:** Control end-effectors (feet, hands) while respecting:
1. Contact constraints (foot must stay on ground)
2. Joint limits and torque limits
3. Balance (ZMP inside support polygon)

**Optimization Problem:**

$$
\begin{aligned}
\min_{\ddot{\mathbf{q}}, \boldsymbol{\tau}, \mathbf{f}} \quad & \| \ddot{\mathbf{x}} - \ddot{\mathbf{x}}^{\text{des}} \|^2 + \lambda \| \boldsymbol{\tau} \|^2 \\
\text{subject to} \quad & \mathbf{M}(\mathbf{q}) \ddot{\mathbf{q}} + \mathbf{h}(\mathbf{q}, \dot{\mathbf{q}}) = \boldsymbol{\tau} + J_c^T \mathbf{f} \\
& J_c \ddot{\mathbf{q}} + \dot{J}_c \dot{\mathbf{q}} = 0 \quad \text{(contact constraint)} \\
& \mathbf{f}_z \geq 0 \quad \text{(unilateral force)} \\
& |\mathbf{f}_x|, |\mathbf{f}_y| \leq \mu \mathbf{f}_z \quad \text{(friction cone)}
\end{aligned}
$$

### Python Implementation with OSQP

```python
import osqp
from scipy import sparse

def whole_body_control(self, x_des, xd_des, xdd_des):
    """
    Quadratic Programming-based WBC

    Args:
        x_des: Desired end-effector position
        xd_des: Desired end-effector velocity
        xdd_des: Desired end-effector acceleration

    Returns:
        tau: Joint torques
    """
    n = self.num_joints
    m = 3  # Contact forces (x, y, z) per foot

    # Current state
    q = self.get_joint_positions()
    qd = self.get_joint_velocities()

    # Dynamics matrices
    M = self.compute_mass_matrix(q)
    h = self.compute_nonlinear_effects(q, qd)  # Coriolis + gravity
    J_foot = self.compute_foot_jacobian(q)
    Jd_foot = self.compute_foot_jacobian_derivative(q, qd)

    # Task Jacobian (end-effector to joints)
    J_task = self.compute_task_jacobian(q)

    # QP matrices
    # min 0.5 x^T P x + q^T x
    # s.t. l <= Ax <= u

    # Decision variables: x = [ddq, tau, f]
    x_dim = n + n + m

    # Cost: ||J*ddq + Jd*qd - xdd_des||^2 + lambda*||tau||^2
    lambda_reg = 0.01

    P = sparse.block_diag([
        J_task.T @ J_task,
        lambda_reg * sparse.eye(n),
        sparse.csc_matrix((m, m))
    ])

    q_vec = np.concatenate([
        -J_task.T @ (xdd_des - Jd_foot @ qd),
        np.zeros(n),
        np.zeros(m)
    ])

    # Equality constraints: M*ddq - tau - J_c^T*f = -h
    A_eq = sparse.hstack([M, -sparse.eye(n), -J_foot.T])
    l_eq = -h
    u_eq = -h

    # Contact constraint: J_c*ddq + Jd_c*qd = 0
    A_contact = sparse.hstack([J_foot, sparse.csc_matrix((3, n)), sparse.csc_matrix((3, m))])
    l_contact = -Jd_foot @ qd
    u_contact = -Jd_foot @ qd

    # Friction cone: |f_x|, |f_y| <= mu*f_z, f_z >= 0
    mu = 0.7  # Friction coefficient
    A_friction = sparse.csc_matrix([
        [1, 0, -mu],   # f_x <= mu*f_z
        [-1, 0, -mu],  # -f_x <= mu*f_z
        [0, 1, -mu],   # f_y <= mu*f_z
        [0, -1, -mu],  # -f_y <= mu*f_z
        [0, 0, -1],    # -f_z <= 0 (f_z >= 0)
    ])
    A_friction = sparse.hstack([
        sparse.csc_matrix((5, n + n)),
        A_friction
    ])
    l_friction = np.array([-np.inf, -np.inf, -np.inf, -np.inf, -np.inf])
    u_friction = np.zeros(5)

    # Stack constraints
    A = sparse.vstack([A_eq, A_contact, A_friction])
    l = np.concatenate([l_eq, l_contact, l_friction])
    u = np.concatenate([u_eq, u_contact, u_friction])

    # Solve QP
    prob = osqp.OSQP()
    prob.setup(P, q_vec, A, l, u, verbose=False)
    res = prob.solve()

    if res.info.status != 'solved':
        print(f"QP failed: {res.info.status}")
        return np.zeros(n)

    # Extract solution
    ddq = res.x[:n]
    tau = res.x[n:2*n]
    f = res.x[2*n:]

    return tau
```

